cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Financial-NRF: A Numerical Reliability Framework for
  Retrieval-Augmented AI Systems
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to its findings, please
  cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aaron Prakash
    family-names: Gandi
    affiliation: Ulster University
repository-code: 'https://github.com/aaronsunny007/Financial-NRF'
abstract: >-
  A measurement framework for retrieval-augmented question
  answering over financial documents. Four independent
  checks - execution accuracy, numerical evidence support,
  gold-free post-hoc arithmetic verification, and confidence
  calibration - are applied to generated answers and
  combined into a composite reliability score. Two
  falsification experiments show that the composite fails to
  track reliability under graded evidence degradation
  (r = -0.10) and inverts the ranking of two systems whose
  true ordering is known, while the individual diagnostic
  components remain informative.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - financial question answering
  - reliability metrics
  - hallucination detection
  - confidence calibration
  - FinQA
license: MIT
